# YouTube Cookies File (Netscape HTTP Cookie Format)
# 
# This file allows yt-dlp to authenticate with YouTube and bypass bot detection.
# 
# HOW TO GET YOUR COOKIES:
# 
# METHOD 1 - Browser Extension (Easiest):
#   1. Install "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY" extension for Chrome/Firefox
#   2. Go to https://youtube.com and login to your Google account
#   3. Click the extension and export cookies
#   4. Copy ALL the content and paste it below (replace these example lines)
#
# METHOD 2 - yt-dlp Command:
#   Run: yt-dlp --cookies-from-browser chrome --cookies youtube_cookies.txt "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ"
#
# DEPLOYMENT:
#   - For Railway/Render: Set YOUTUBE_COOKIES environment variable with file contents
#   - For local: Save this file as "youtube_cookies.txt" (remove .example)
#
# SECURITY:
#   - Never commit this file to git (already in .gitignore)
#   - Cookies expire every 6 months - update when needed
#   - Use a dedicated Google account for better security
#
# ============================================
# Paste your actual YouTube cookies below:
# ============================================

# Netscape HTTP Cookie File
# This is a generated file. Do not edit.

# Example format (replace with your actual cookies):
# .youtube.com	TRUE	/	TRUE	1234567890	VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE	your_cookie_value_here
# .youtube.com	TRUE	/	FALSE	1234567890	YSC	your_cookie_value_here
# .youtube.com	TRUE	/	TRUE	1234567890	PREF	your_cookie_value_here

